# Keep the build context tiny (the legacy builder re-uploads it every build):
# ignore everything, then re-include only what the sandbox Dockerfile COPYs:
#   - docker/ — the extra-ca certs and any .sh/.py scripts (entrypoint, impact CLI)
#   - experiments/picocli-putValue/stripped/ — the STUB fixture, used ONLY by the
#     discarded gradle-warm stage to download deps (the warmed ~/.gradle is what
#     ends up in the image; the stub source does NOT). The original/reference
#     solution is NEVER included in the context.
# The globs auto-include new scripts so a future COPY can't silently break the
# build (as adding sandbox-entrypoint.sh / impact_cli.py did). __pycache__ etc.
# stay excluded.
*
!docker
docker/*
!docker/extra-ca
!docker/*.sh
!docker/*.py
# Runtime-probe agent SOURCE (built into the image by Dockerfile.sandbox). A new
# subdir is NOT auto-included by the *.sh/*.py globs, so re-include it explicitly;
# keep build artefacts out of the context.
!docker/runtime-probe
!docker/runtime-probe/**
docker/runtime-probe/build
docker/runtime-probe/.gradle
docker/runtime-probe/recorder/build
docker/runtime-probe/recorder/.gradle
# Build context for the gradle-warm stage: ONLY the stripped (stub) fixture.
!experiments
experiments/*
!experiments/picocli-putValue
experiments/picocli-putValue/*
!experiments/picocli-putValue/stripped
!experiments/picocli-putValue/stripped/**
